<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace (Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult)",
        "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace faithfully reproduces Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py> ;
    schema:about "Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Volkening & Sandstede (2015/2018) simulations or their parameter values; quantitative iridophore density, sheet correlation length or S/L switching rates measured in vivo; fin (as opposed to trunk flank) patterning; the 3V stripe of large adults; the Danio species variability of Volkening & Sandstede (2018)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 3x3 Nakamasu Jacobian, Routh-Hurwitz invariants, dispersion curve and a DCT-II IMEX 2D 3-species PDE with saturating synthesis (Sections 2-3); in silico Fig. 2 / Fig. 3 ablations (Section 4); leopard sweep and dual negative controls (Section 5); specimen segmentation (Section 6)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Lean 4 Theorems 1-6 for the integer kernels of the laws above",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 5b hybrid model: Lagrangian growing-flank PDE with dilution and D/g^2 diffusion, point iridophore agents with S/L state, density-limited proliferation, state-dependent random walk, sigmoidal S<->L switching on u - v, anisotropic (x-coherent) density kernel feeding back on the continuum; ontogeny record of stripe count vs standard length; controls and sweeps",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009): short-range mutual melanophore-xanthophore repulsion plus long-range xanthophore-to-melanophore survival support form a Turing network; xanthophore interstripe ablation kills >45% of flanked melanophores (Fig. 2); regeneration orientation follows intact boundaries (Fig. 3)",
        "reported_in_source: Parichy et al. (2009): post-embryonic stage anchors PB 7.2, PR 8.6, SP 9.6, J 10.4, J+ 11.0, J++ 13.0 mm SL",
        "reported_in_source: Singh et al. (2014), Frohnhöfer et al. (2013), Patterson & Parichy (2013): iridophores appear on the horizontal myoseptum (X0), proliferate as a dense sheet, disperse as loose cells over stripes and re-aggregate at the next interstripes; dense iridophores promote xanthophores and exclude melanophores; iridophore-less shady mutants lack organized stripes",
        "reported_in_source: Volkening & Sandstede (2015, 2018): agent-based melanophores/xanthophores on a growing domain add stripes sequentially; iridophores in dense (interstripe) and loose (stripe) forms switch shape according to the local melanophore/xanthophore environment and make stripe formation robust",
        "transfer_boundary: Growth is isometric and uniform; the standard-length axis is a linear map SL = 7.2 g / 0.4 with no allometry; stripe insertion happens by splitting of stretched stripes rather than by marginal addition, and symmetrically (X1D and X1V together) rather than ventral-first",
        "transfer_boundary: Panel B and the Fig. 3 regeneration experiment still use the cos(k_c y) whole-flank template cue",
        "transfer_boundary: The hybrid model is a REDUCED version of Volkening & Sandstede: melanophores and xanthophores remain continuum fields (no birth/death agent rules), only iridophores are discrete, and the switching rule is a sigmoid of the continuum difference u - v rather than counts of neighbouring cells",
        "transfer_boundary: The normal-table stripe counts in iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json are approximate readings (+/- 1 stripe) of published descriptions, not digitized data" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py; output: docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_comparison.png; organism: Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/3aaa03d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 53d32e73f4ffa155070025683029f96e36562f3bf4bf95b4d073d237a096b1d2; artifact_sha256: 9872965ba333bb85861de6bafbcc286f1a6c6906a2e4d4ba18a19ca84cb6f3b3; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/danio_rerio_specimen.jpg=850b2d4a94c7cbcb..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json=c25943ac48e02adf..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/paper_citations.bib=4b64e2dc8820bfad..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/scout_manifest.json=4a8716bc59f35f30..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_reference.json=716558fb68296749...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009): short-range mutual melanophore-xanthophore repulsion plus long-range xanthophore-to-melanophore survival support form a Turing network; xanthophore interstripe ablation kills >45% of flanked melanophores (Fig. 2); regeneration orientation follows intact boundaries (Fig. 3) | Volkening & Sandstede (2015, 2018): agent-based melanophores/xanthophores on a growing domain add stripes sequentially; iridophores in dense (interstripe) and loose (stripe) forms switch shape according to the local melanophore/xanthophore environment and make stripe formation robust | Singh et al. (2014), Frohnhöfer et al. (2013), Patterson & Parichy (2013): iridophores appear on the horizontal myoseptum (X0), proliferate as a dense sheet, disperse as loose cells over stripes and re-aggregate at the next interstripes; dense iridophores promote xanthophores and exclude melanophores; iridophore-less shady mutants lack organized stripes | Parichy et al. (2009): post-embryonic stage anchors PB 7.2, PR 8.6, SP 9.6, J 10.4, J+ 11.0, J++ 13.0 mm SL; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 3x3 Nakamasu Jacobian, Routh-Hurwitz invariants, dispersion curve and a DCT-II IMEX 2D 3-species PDE with saturating synthesis (Sections 2-3); in silico Fig. 2 / Fig. 3 ablations (Section 4); leopard sweep and dual negative controls (Section 5); specimen segmentation (Section 6) | Section 5b hybrid model: Lagrangian growing-flank PDE with dilution and D/g^2 diffusion, point iridophore agents with S/L state, density-limited proliferation, state-dependent random walk, sigmoidal S<->L switching on u - v, anisotropic (x-coherent) density kernel feeding back on the continuum; ontogeny record of stripe count vs standard length; controls and sweeps | Lean 4 Theorems 1-6 for the integer kernels of the laws above; transfer_boundary: The hybrid model is a REDUCED version of Volkening & Sandstede: melanophores and xanthophores remain continuum fields (no birth/death agent rules), only iridophores are discrete, and the switching rule is a sigmoid of the continuum difference u - v rather than counts of neighbouring cells | Growth is isometric and uniform; the standard-length axis is a linear map SL = 7.2 g / 0.4 with no allometry; stripe insertion happens by splitting of stretched stripes rather than by marginal addition, and symmetrically (X1D and X1V together) rather than ventral-first | The normal-table stripe counts in iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json are approximate readings (+/- 1 stripe) of published descriptions, not digitized data | Panel B and the Fig. 3 regeneration experiment still use the cos(k_c y) whole-flank template cue; does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Volkening & Sandstede (2015/2018) simulations or their parameter values; quantitative iridophore density, sheet correlation length or S/L switching rates measured in vivo; fin (as opposed to trunk flank) patterning; the 3V stripe of large adults; the Danio species variability of Volkening & Sandstede (2018)]" ;
