    schema:about "Zebrafish (Danio rerio) melanophore-xanthophore-iridophore flank stripes, juvenile (stage PB) to adult" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Volkening & Sandstede (2015/2018) simulations or their parameter values; quantitative iridophore density, sheet correlation length or S/L switching rates measured in vivo; fin (as opposed to trunk flank) patterning; the 3V stripe of large adults; the Danio species variability of Volkening & Sandstede (2018)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 3x3 Nakamasu Jacobian, Routh-Hurwitz invariants, dispersion curve and a DCT-II IMEX 2D 3-species PDE with saturating synthesis (Sections 2-3); in silico Fig. 2 / Fig. 3 ablations (Section 4); leopard sweep and dual negative controls (Section 5); specimen segmentation (Section 6)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Lean 4 Theorems 1-6 for the integer kernels of the laws above",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Section 5b hybrid model: Lagrangian growing-flank PDE with dilution and D/g^2 diffusion, point iridophore agents with S/L state, density-limited proliferation, state-dependent random walk, sigmoidal S<->L switching on u - v, anisotropic (x-coherent) density kernel feeding back on the continuum; ontogeny record of stripe count vs standard length; controls and sweeps",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009): short-range mutual melanophore-xanthophore repulsion plus long-range xanthophore-to-melanophore survival support form a Turing network; xanthophore interstripe ablation kills >45% of flanked melanophores (Fig. 2); regeneration orientation follows intact boundaries (Fig. 3)",
        "reported_in_source: Parichy et al. (2009): post-embryonic stage anchors PB 7.2, PR 8.6, SP 9.6, J 10.4, J+ 11.0, J++ 13.0 mm SL",
        "reported_in_source: Singh et al. (2014), Frohnhöfer et al. (2013), Patterson & Parichy (2013): iridophores appear on the horizontal myoseptum (X0), proliferate as a dense sheet, disperse as loose cells over stripes and re-aggregate at the next interstripes; dense iridophores promote xanthophores and exclude melanophores; iridophore-less shady mutants lack organized stripes",
        "reported_in_source: Volkening & Sandstede (2015, 2018): agent-based melanophores/xanthophores on a growing domain add stripes sequentially; iridophores in dense (interstripe) and loose (stripe) forms switch shape according to the local melanophore/xanthophore environment and make stripe formation robust",
        "transfer_boundary: Growth is isometric and uniform; the standard-length axis is a linear map SL = 7.2 g / 0.4 with no allometry; stripe insertion happens by splitting of stretched stripes rather than by marginal addition, and symmetrically (X1D and X1V together) rather than ventral-first",
        "transfer_boundary: Panel B and the Fig. 3 regeneration experiment still use the cos(k_c y) whole-flank template cue",
        "transfer_boundary: The hybrid model is a REDUCED version of Volkening & Sandstede: melanophores and xanthophores remain continuum fields (no birth/death agent rules), only iridophores are discrete, and the switching rule is a sigmoid of the continuum difference u - v rather than counts of neighbouring cells",
        "transfer_boundary: The normal-table stripe counts in iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json are approximate readings (+/- 1 stripe) of published descriptions, not digitized data" ;
