<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Section 5b banner (L565-590) maps every agent rule to its source (Volkening & Sandstede 2015/2018, Singh 2014, Frohnhöfer 2013, Patterson & Parichy 2013, Parichy 2009, Crampin 1999) and to Lean Theorems 4-6; the math KG spec registers the three new laws with Lean loci and code loci; the docstring lists the known residuals. Deductions: the calibration constants (gamma_u 0.10, gamma_v 0.03, gamma_L 0.02, rho_ref 30, step_S/step_L, p_div, kernel sigmas, switch threshold 0.10) have no cited origin and are only described as calibration (-5); the stripe counter and juvenile-count heuristics (L605-634) are uncited conventions (-2); Panel B's template cue is disclosed on the panel but the Fig. 3 regeneration template at L468 is not (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py L655–L668: Hybrid calibration defaults (gamma_*, step_*, p_div_*, rho_ref, kernel sigmas) without cited values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L655-L668>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Nakamasu core (exact J0, Routh-Hurwitz, dispersion, saturating 3-species PDE, L153-388) and the laser-ablation reproductions (L394-492) are unchanged and remain faithful. The remediation adds the requested mechanism in recognisable Volkening & Sandstede form: discrete iridophores with S/L state, environment-dependent switching, proliferation, dispersal and feedback, on a growing domain whose Lagrangian PDE carries the correct -2 (g'/g) u dilution and D/g^2 scaling (L778-786). Deductions: the whole-flank cos(k_c y) template that drives Panel B and the Fig. 3 regeneration run (L308-309, L468) imposes the 5-stripe count and orientation that v2 credited as emergent (-3); the iridophore rules are reduced (sigmoid of the continuum u - v instead of neighbour counts; no melanophore/xanthophore agents, no long-range iridophore -> melanophore term) (-3); gamma_u/gamma_v/gamma_L, rho_ref, step and division rates and the x-coherent kernel are calibration choices without source values, and the parallel-insertion outcome depends on that kernel (-3); insertion is by splitting of stretched stripes and symmetric, unlike the ventral-first marginal addition in vivo (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py L308–L309: Whole-flank cue_profile = myoseptum_cue * cos(k_c (y - L_y/2)) still templates Panel B; L468 repeats it for the Fig. 3 regeneration run — stripe count/orientation imposed, not emergent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L308-L309>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1396-1553) now returns 14 measurements: the 8 Pass 2 ones plus the hybrid adult stripe count vs the normal table (4 vs 4-5), SL at first insertion (13.5 mm vs J 10.4 mm), dense-iridophore interstripe occupancy (1.00 vs >= 0.85), iridophore-less control anisotropy (1.01 vs 1.0 isotropic reference), Turing-band mode count (9, Lean Theorem 4) and the hybrid anti-phase correlation (-0.9995). Deductions: the normal-table stripe counts are approximate (+/- 1) readings and not digitized data (-4); the first-insertion SL misses its reference by ~3 mm and the asymmetry (ventral-first) is not measured (-3); S/L occupancy and the shady-like control are compared with qualitative statements, not measured fractions (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json L60–L72: Stage-anchored stripe-count normal table with confidence_note declaring +/- 1 approximate readings <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json#L60-L72>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-measurement-2d-pde-melanophore-xanthophore-anti-phase-pearson-correlation-r-uv>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-measurement-3-species-turing-critical-wavenumber-k-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-measurement-characteristic-zebrafish-stripe-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-measurement-dense-s-iridophore-interstripe-occupancy-fraction-at-adult-stage>,
