<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — MorphoEval overall 90.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py` (overall weighted score: 90.6 / 100, down 1.5 points from 92.1 in Pass 2 because the round exposed two defects that the Pass 2 scores had credited). The single Pass 2 remediation item is closed: Section 5b couples the Nakamasu (u, v, w) continuum PDE to discrete dense/loose iridophore agents (reduced Volkening & Sandstede 2018 rules) on an isometrically growing flank (stage PB, SL 7.2 mm -> SL 18 mm) with the Crampin-Gaffney-Maini dilution term; the X0 cue now emerges from agents seeded on the myoseptum instead of a whole-flank cos(k_c y) template, stripes are inserted sequentially 2 -> 4 (parallel, anisotropy 30.2; 3/3 seeds aligned) with dense iridophores colonizing the new X1D/X1V interstripes (100% of S agents in interstripes, 68% of L agents in stripes), the iridophore-less control is isotropic (anisotropy 1.01, shady-like) and the static adult-size control is less aligned (8.4) than the growing flank; six new reference-backed measurements, five new self-test checks and Lean Theorems 4-6 (+2 lemmas, 0 sorrys) back the new mathematics. Exposed defects: the v2 wild-type panel and the Fig. 3 regeneration experiment are template-cued over the whole flank (their stripe count/orientation is imposed), the v2 CLI flags were never wired to the computation, the hybrid insertion is symmetric and late (SL 13.5 vs ~10.4-11.0 mm) and depends on a calibrated x-coherent iridophore kernel. Overall 90.6/100 (faithfulness 89.7, reproducibility 92.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3aaa03d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py at 3aaa03d, image/png, 1240926 B, 2400×1960 px, artifact_sha256 9872965ba333bb85861de6bafbcc286f1a6c6906a2e4d4ba18a19ca84cb6f3b3 (sha256 9872965ba333bb85861de6bafbcc286f1a6c6906a2e4d4ba18a19ca84cb6f3b3), spec_fingerprint 53d32e73f4ffa155070025683029f96e36562f3bf4bf95b4d073d237a096b1d2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 53d32e73f4ffa155070025683029f96e36562f3bf4bf95b4d073d237a096b1d2; artifact_sha256: 9872965ba333bb85861de6bafbcc286f1a6c6906a2e4d4ba18a19ca84cb6f3b3; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/danio_rerio_specimen.jpg=850b2d4a94c7cbcb..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json=c25943ac48e02adf..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/paper_citations.bib=4b64e2dc8820bfad..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/scout_manifest.json=4a8716bc59f35f30..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_reference.json=716558fb68296749...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009): short-range mutual melanophore-xanthophore repulsion plus long-range xanthophore-to-melanophore survival support form a Turing network; xanthophore interstripe ablation kills >45% of flanked melanophores (Fig. 2); regeneration orientation follows intact boundaries (Fig. 3) | Volkening & Sandstede (2015, 2018): agent-based melanophores/xanthophores on a growing domain add stripes sequentially; iridophores in dense (interstripe) and loose (stripe) forms switch shape according to the local melanophore/xanthophore environment and make stripe formation robust | Singh et al. (2014), Frohnhöfer et al. (2013), Patterson & Parichy (2013): iridophores appear on the horizontal myoseptum (X0), proliferate as a dense sheet, disperse as loose cells over stripes and re-aggregate at the next interstripes; dense iridophores promote xanthophores and exclude melanophores; iridophore-less shady mutants lack organized stripes | Parichy et al. (2009): post-embryonic stage anchors PB 7.2, PR 8.6, SP 9.6, J 10.4, J+ 11.0, J++ 13.0 mm SL; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 3x3 Nakamasu Jacobian, Routh-Hurwitz invariants, dispersion curve and a DCT-II IMEX 2D 3-species PDE with saturating synthesis (Sections 2-3); in silico Fig. 2 / Fig. 3 ablations (Section 4); leopard sweep and dual negative controls (Section 5); specimen segmentation (Section 6) | Section 5b hybrid model: Lagrangian growing-flank PDE with dilution and D/g^2 diffusion, point iridophore agents with S/L state, density-limited proliferation, state-dependent random walk, sigmoidal S<->L switching on u - v, anisotropic (x-coherent) density kernel feeding back on the continuum; ontogeny record of stripe count vs standard length; controls and sweeps | Lean 4 Theorems 1-6 for the integer kernels of the laws above; transfer_boundary: The hybrid model is a REDUCED version of Volkening & Sandstede: melanophores and xanthophores remain continuum fields (no birth/death agent rules), only iridophores are discrete, and the switching rule is a sigmoid of the continuum difference u - v rather than counts of neighbouring cells | Growth is isometric and uniform; the standard-length axis is a linear map SL = 7.2 g / 0.4 with no allometry; stripe insertion happens by splitting of stretched stripes rather than by marginal addition, and symmetrically (X1D and X1V together) rather than ventral-first | The normal-table stripe counts in iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json are approximate readings (+/- 1 stripe) of published descriptions, not digitized data | Panel B and the Fig. 3 regeneration experiment still use the cos(k_c y) whole-flank template cue; does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Volkening & Sandstede (2015/2018) simulations or their parameter values; quantitative iridophore density, sheet correlation length or S/L switching rates measured in vivo; fin (as opposed to trunk flank) patterning; the 3V stripe of large adults; the Danio species variability of Volkening & Sandstede (2018)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:1660-1726 — `--variant` prints a JSON summary but does not render; add `--out PATH` so a non-default parameter set (e.g. --n-irid 0, --growth-fraction 0.0) produces a flank image, and show at least one rendered flank per growth schedule in Panel J.",
        "remediation needed: 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:308-309 and 468 — the whole-flank template cue cos(k_c (y - L_y/2)) still drives Panel B (`integrate_nakamasu_pde_2d`, myoseptum_cue = 0.22) and the Fig. 3 regeneration run (0.14 amplitude), imposing the 5-stripe count and the horizontal orientation that the regeneration anisotropy (7.38) then reports. Replace both with the agent-derived X0 cue of Section 5b (or a cue confined to |y - L_y/2| < lambda_c/4) and re-measure the Fig. 3 regeneration anisotropy without the template.",
        "remediation needed: 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:636-898 — insertion is dorsoventrally symmetric (X1D and X1V appear together at SL 13.5 mm) and proceeds by splitting of stretched stripes, whereas in vivo X1V/2V precede X1D/2D (~10.4-11.0 mm) and new stripes are added at the margins. Add a ventral-first bias (e.g. ventral dispersal/aggregation bias of loose iridophores, Singh 2014) or a marginal-growth variant, and measure the SL of the first ventral vs dorsal insertion separately against the normal table.",
        "remediation needed: 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:727-744 and 655-668 — the x-coherent dense iridophore kernel (kernel_sigma_x = 1.2 vs kernel_sigma = 0.3) is the calibration that makes insertion parallel; with an isotropic kernel about half of the seeds produced labyrinthine insertions (documented in the function docstring only). Quantify this with a kernel-anisotropy sweep reporting the aligned-seed fraction, and anchor kernel_sigma_x to a measured along-interstripe correlation length of dense iridophore sheets (Singh 2014 Fig. 1-2 images) or derive it from an agent adhesion rule.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/iridophore_ontogeny_reference.json:60-72 and 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:1409-1429 — the normal-table stripe counts are approximate (+/- 1) readings. Digitize quantitative stripe/interstripe counts vs SL from Parichy et al. (2009) or Frohnhöfer et al. (2013) Fig. 1 / Volkening & Sandstede (2015) Fig. 4, store them with page/figure pins, and tighten the two ontogeny measurements to those values.",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean:176-205 and 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py:781-783 — Theorem 5 checks a single dilution value (r = 0.1) on the Routh-Hurwitz invariants; add a theorem on the IMEX denominators 1 + dt (c + r + D k^2) >= 1 for all r, k^2 >= 0 (unconditional stability of the implicit step on the growing domain) and a general-r Routh-Hurwitz lemma rather than the r = 1 instance." ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.06e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The leopard sweep and dual negative controls (L499-562) are retained; Pass 3 adds a growth-rate sweep (3 schedules), the iridophore-less, static-domain and no-switch controls and a 3-seed robustness check (L901-942), and the CLI is now actually wired: `--variant` runs the template PDE and the hybrid model with every kinetic and hybrid flag and prints a JSON summary (L1660-1726). Deductions: the v2 CLI parsed its flags but `main()` ignored them, so the v2 \"exposes full CLI flags\" credit was unearned (-3); the growth sweep behaves monotonically (faster growth delays the first insertion: SL 16.9 / 13.5 / 13.4 mm for fast / default / slow) but is shown only as stripe count vs SL with no rendered flanks along the sweep, and the kernel-anisotropy and feedback-strength calibrations are not swept at all (-4); `--variant` does not render a figure, so non-default parameter sets cannot be inspected visually (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py L1273–L1296: Panel J plots only stripe count vs SL per growth schedule; no rendered flanks along the sweep <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L1273-L1296>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seeds for both the PDE noise and the agent RNG (bitwise two-run determinism of fields, states and positions is checked, L1642-1647); the 13-check `--self-test` runs in ~32 s and the default render in 13-25 s, well under the 3-minute budget; outputs are self-contained (12-panel PNG + 8-frame GIF); the environment is recorded above. Deductions: no requirements lock file is vendored for this slot (-3); the self-test thresholds for the hybrid (anisotropy > 5, aligned fraction >= 2/3, SL_first in [11, 16]) are tuned to the default seed set (-2); the README in the dataset directory documents the files but the top-level README section was not updated (outside this loop's allowed files) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
