<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Panel I shows an emergent (not templated) adult flank with 4 dark stripes separated by 3 interstripes whose dense iridophores sit in the light bands — the same 4-stripe count the specimen segmentation finds (Panel F, L954-1030) and a plausible rendering of the X0/X1D/X1V sheets of Frohnhöfer 2013 / Singh 2014; Panels E-G keep the SHA-256-locked Danio rerio photograph, its segmented stripes and the standardized profile comparison. Deductions: no juvenile-stage specimen images are vendored, so the 2 -> 4 ontogeny is compared with a qualitative normal table rather than with pictures (-5); dense iridophore coverage of X1D/X1V is sparse compared with the contiguous sheets seen in vivo, and loose iridophores are few (loose fraction 0.02) (-3); the GIF is the model alone with no specimen frame (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
