<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu (2009) Short-Range Melanophore-Xanthophore Mutual Repulsion Saddle Instability" ;
    dct:description "Proves that two mutually repressing pigment cell populations form an effective local positive-feedback switch (det J_uv = -1.61 < 0, lambda_anti = +0.70 > 0) without requiring direct single-cell autocatalysis | Variables: u: melanophore density; v: xanthophore density; c_u, c_v: intrinsic clearance rates; b_u = -r_u < 0, a_v = -r_v < 0: short-range contact-mediated mutual repression rates" ;
    dct:source "Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106(21):8429-8434 Fig. 4D & SI Text Eqs. (1)-(6)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L112-L195>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L19-L47> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def short_range_det_uv (cu cv ru rv : Int) : Int := cu * cv - ru * rv
def anti_phase_growth_rate (cu ru : Int) : Int := ru - cu
theorem nakamasu_short_range_mutual_repulsion_instability (cu cv : Int)
    (hcu : cu ≥ 1) (hcv : cv ≥ 1) :
    short_range_det_uv cu cv 0 0 ≥ 1 ∧
    short_range_det_uv 8 8 15 15 = -161 ∧
    anti_phase_growth_rate 8 15 = 7 := by
  unfold short_range_det_uv anti_phase_growth_rate
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide⟩
  have h1 : (1 : Int) * 1 ≤ cu * cv := Int.mul_le_mul hcu hcv (by decide) (by omega)
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "det(J_{uv}) = c_u c_v - b_u a_v < 0  ∧  λ_{anti} = |b_u| - c_u > 0  when  |b_u|, |a_v| > c_u, c_v" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.short_range_det_uv" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.nakamasu_short_range_mutual_repulsion_instability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Long-Range Xanthophore->Melanophore Survival Factor Routh-Hurwitz Homogeneous Stabilization" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the long-range xanthophore-to-melanophore survival pathway v -> w -> u stabilizes the homogeneous 3-cell equilibrium at k = 0 despite the local (u, v) saddle instability | Variables: w: long-range diffusible factor secreted by xanthophores (b_w = 1.20 > 0) promoting melanophore survival (d_u = 1.20 > 0); p_1, p_2, p_3: Routh-Hurwitz cubic coefficients of J_0" ;
    dct:source "Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106(21):8429-8434 Figs. 2, 4D & SI Text" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L125-L210>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L54-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem nakamasu_long_range_factor_routh_hurwitz_stabilization :
    routh_hurwitz_p1 8 8 9 = 25 ∧
    routh_hurwitz_p2 8 8 9 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12 = 163 ∧
    routh_hurwitz_p3 8 8 9 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12 = 2961 ∧
    (routh_hurwitz_p1 8 8 9) * (routh_hurwitz_p2 8 8 9 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12)
      - (routh_hurwitz_p3 8 8 9 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12) = 1114 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p_1 = -tr(J_0) = 2.50 > 0,  p_2 = 1.63 > 0,  p_3 = -det(J_0) = 2.961 > 0,  p_1 p_2 - p_3 = 1.114 > 0  ⟹  Re λ(J_0) < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.routh_hurwitz_p3" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.nakamasu_long_range_factor_routh_hurwitz_stabilization" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Fast-Diffusing Long-Range Factor (D_w ≫ D_u, D_v) Bounded Turing Stripe Instability Theorem" ;
    dct:description "Proves that differential long-range signaling range D_w / D_u = 25 opens a finite stationary Turing band around k_c = 3.4106 (lambda_c = 1.8423), while equal diffusion quenches pattern formation | Variables: q = k^2: squared spatial wavenumber; D_u = D_v = 0.02: short-range pigment cell motility/projection scale; D_w = 0.50: long-range factor diffusivity" ;
    dct:source "Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106(21):8429-8434 Fig. 5 & SI Text" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L155-L235>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L85-L120> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem nakamasu_diffusive_turing_band_and_ablation_collapse :
    p3_dispersive 0 2 2 50 = 2961000 ∧
    p3_dispersive 12 2 2 50 = -3219960 ∧
    p3_dispersive 35 2 2 50 = 5670000 ∧
    p3_dispersive 12 2 2 2 = 3510024 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p_3(q) = -det(J_0 - q D) < 0  for  q = k^2 ∈ (4.4663, 28.8036)  at  D_w / D_u = 25,  whereas  p_3(q) > 0  for all  q ≥ 0  at  D_w = D_u = D_v" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.p3_dispersive" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.nakamasu_diffusive_turing_band_and_ablation_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Growing-Domain Neumann Mode Insertion Across the Nakamasu Turing Band" ;
    dct:description "Explains why the 2-stripe juvenile pattern (1D, 1V around X0) cannot persist as a single mode on the adult flank and must insert new stripes (X1D/2D, X1V/2V) during growth; parity-checked in self_test check 9 and the hybrid ontogeny record | Variables: n: Neumann cosine mode index (n half-waves ≈ n/2 dark stripes); L: dorsoventral flank height (3.68 juvenile at SL 7.2 mm, 9.2 adult at SL 18 mm); integer scalings k×1e4, π×1e5, L×10" ;
    dct:source "Nakamasu et al. (2009) Fig. 5 band; Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull Math Biol 61:1093 (growing-domain mode insertion); Parichy et al. (2009) Dev Dyn 238:2975 stage anchors" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L612-L621>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L144-L173> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def mode_in_turing_band (n L10 : Int) : Bool :=
  decide (21134 * L10 ≤ n * 314159 ∧ n * 314159 ≤ 53669 * L10)
theorem nakamasu_growing_domain_stripe_insertion :
    mode_in_turing_band 4 37 = true ∧ mode_in_turing_band 10 37 = false ∧
    mode_in_turing_band 4 92 = false ∧ mode_in_turing_band 6 92 = false ∧
    mode_in_turing_band 7 92 = true ∧ mode_in_turing_band 10 92 = true ∧
    mode_in_turing_band 15 92 = true ∧ mode_in_turing_band 16 92 = false := by decide
theorem mode_in_turing_band_scales (n L10 : Int) :
    mode_in_turing_band (2 * n) (2 * L10) = mode_in_turing_band n L10
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "mode cos(n π y / L) ∈ Turing band ⟺ k_min L ≤ n π ≤ k_max L, k ∈ [2.1134, 5.3669];  L = 3.68: n ∈ [3, 6] (n = 4 ↔ 2 stripes);  L = 9.2: n ∈ [7, 15] (n = 10 ↔ 5 stripes);  no n is admissible at both sizes ⟹ isometric growth forces stripe insertion" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.mode_in_turing_band" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.nakamasu_growing_domain_stripe_insertion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Growth Dilution Preserves Routh-Hurwitz Homogeneous Stability and the Short-Range Saddle" ;
    dct:description "Shows the growing-domain correction (Crampin-Gaffney-Maini 1999) used by the hybrid solver cannot destabilize the homogeneous state nor remove the local (u, v) saddle that drives segregation; parity-checked in self_test check 10 via compute_nakamasu_theory(c_u=0.9, c_v=0.9, c_w=1.0) | Variables: r = 2 g'/g: dilution rate of a uniformly (isotropically) growing 2D domain; the script's maximum is 2·(0.6/153.6)/0.4 = 0.0195 ≪ 0.1; c_u, c_v, c_w each shifted by r" ;
    dct:source "Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull Math Biol 61:1093-1120; Nakamasu et al. (2009) SI Text" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L778-L786>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L176-L205> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem nakamasu_growth_dilution_preserves_routh_hurwitz :
    routh_hurwitz_p1 9 9 10 = 28 ∧
    routh_hurwitz_p2 9 9 10 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12 = 216 ∧
    routh_hurwitz_p3 9 9 10 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12 = 3150 ∧
    (routh_hurwitz_p1 9 9 10) * (routh_hurwitz_p2 9 9 10 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12)
      - (routh_hurwitz_p3 9 9 10 (-15) 12 (-15) (-6) (-9) 12) = 2898 ∧
    short_range_det_uv 9 9 15 15 = -144 := by decide
theorem dilution_raises_p1 (cu cv cw r : Int) (hr : r ≥ 0) :
    routh_hurwitz_p1 (cu + r) (cv + r) (cw + r) = routh_hurwitz_p1 cu cv cw + 3 * r ∧
    routh_hurwitz_p1 (cu + r) (cv + r) (cw + r) ≥ routh_hurwitz_p1 cu cv cw
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Lagrangian growing-domain Jacobian J0 − r I, r = 2 g'/g ≥ 0 (isotropic dilution): at r = 0.1, p1 = 2.80 > 0, p2 = 2.16 > 0, p3 = 3.150 > 0, p1 p2 − p3 = 2.898 > 0, det(J_uv) = 0.81 − 2.25 = −1.44 < 0;  p1(r) = p1(0) + 3r" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.routh_hurwitz_p1" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.nakamasu_growth_dilution_preserves_routh_hurwitz" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Iridophore Dense<->Loose Switching Rule Is Exclusive and Conserves Agents" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the reduced Volkening & Sandstede (2018) shape-transition rule used for every agent update: a cell never receives contradictory instructions and switching never creates or destroys iridophores (only proliferation does); parity-checked in self_test check 13 | Variables: d = u − v: local melanophore excess at the agent position; θ = 0.10: switching threshold; s, l: dense/loose agent counts; a, b: S→L and L→S events per step" ;
    dct:source "Volkening & Sandstede (2018) Nat Commun 9:3231 (iridophore S/L transitions); Singh et al. (2014) Nat Cell Biol 16:607; Frohnhoefer et al. (2013) Development 140:2997" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L802-L812>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_007_zebrafish_three_cell_stripes.lean#L208-L231> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def switch_S_to_L (d θ : Int) : Bool := decide (d > θ)
def switch_L_to_S (d θ : Int) : Bool := decide (-d > θ)
theorem iridophore_switch_exclusive_and_conservative (d θ s l a b : Int) (hθ : θ ≥ 0) :
    ¬ (switch_S_to_L d θ = true ∧ switch_L_to_S d θ = true) ∧
    (s - a + b) + (l + a - b) = s + l
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "S→L iff u − v > θ;  L→S iff v − u > θ;  θ ≥ 0 ⟹ ¬(S→L ∧ L→S);  (s − a + b) + (l + a − b) = s + l" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb2955>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.embor.7400757>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0607790104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2015.0812>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1212821>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.096719>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003561> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cell-Cell Contact Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.switch_S_to_L" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_007.iridophore_switch_exclusive_and_conservative" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

